"The merge/vote ACs describe outcomes evaluated on the Gerrit ticket, not repo artifacts, yet none carry the [operator-attested] tag that would justify attestation-based evidence."],"finding":"Several acceptance criteria depend on an external Gerrit outcome or a future genuine docs-only change occurring, but are not tagged [operator-attested], so their in-session measurability is unclear.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2d2f9536bb282c36","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria: 'Gerrit LLM-Review reaches +1', 'Gerrit Verified reaches +1', 'The change merges before this ticket closes', 'A genuine docs-only Gerrit timing and runner-occupancy comparison is recorded'","norm_id":"n39ecaa263a4aed96","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["No genuine docs-only change lands during the session, leaving the timing-comparison AC unfulfillable in-session."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Prefix the Gerrit-vote, merge, and timing-comparison ACs with `[operator-attested]` and name the recorded attestation (e.g. the docs-only change id and its Verified/+1 vote plus the wall-clock/runner-occupancy figures vs change 1778).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the changed-path classifier decision runs from TRUSTED main-branch code (mirroring the vote job's sparse-checkout-from-main pattern) and obtains the patchset's changed-path list without executing patchset-controlled logic.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gerrit-verify.yaml vote job comment: 'the vote decision must never run patchset-controlled code ... keeping the decision logic trusted also stops a change from voting itself Verified'; it sparse-checks-out scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py from main via actions/checkout, not the patchset","The classifier's SELECT decision gates whether mutation/optionality/matrix/eval/golden-path/identity run at all — a strictly higher-impact decision than the vote normalization","Plan calls the classifier 'deterministic' and 'fail-closed' but never states it must execute from trusted (main-branch) code, nor how it reads the changed-path list without running patchset-controlled classifier logic"],"finding":"The classifier's trust boundary is unspecified: a patchset-controlled classifier could let a hostile docs-only-looking change skip the entire full suite (mutation/tests/optionality/etc.), contradicting the existing vote-job design that runs decision logic only from trusted main.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb87de7939ccc7df8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan: 'Add a deterministic changed-path classifier for the exact Gerrit patchset'; AC 'A change limited to allowlisted documentation paths selects the docs-only lane'","norm_id":"nc873c38b646cfacc","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A hostile or buggy patchset adds a classifier script (or manipulates diff-derived inputs) so it is judged docs-only and skips the code gates that would have caught it"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have the routing job sparse-checkout the classifier script from main (persist-credentials:false), derive the changed-path set from a trusted git-diff of the patchset revision, and feed only that path list into the trusted classifier — never run a classifier script taken from the patchset tree.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a step to EXTRACT the current inline documentation gates out of the _build-and-test.yml pytest matrix job into a single reusable docs-gate definition that BOTH lanes invoke, so 'reuse the same definition' is literally true rather than a re-copy.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_build-and-test.yml `test` job contains the ADR-number, ADR-index, docs-index, README-quickstart, CLI-reference, MCP-reference, and env-var-registry gates as steps interleaved with module-size, pandoc, public-types, MCP-model-schema, config-read gates AND the two pytest runs","There is no standalone docs-gate job or reusable workflow today; 'reuse the same definition' cannot be satisfied literally without first factoring those steps out of the matrix job"],"finding":"The plan's 'reuse a single documentation-gate definition shared with the full lane' presumes an extractable shared docs-gate unit, but today the doc gates are inline steps inside the pytest `test` matrix job (interleaved with code-only gates and pytest itself); the plan does not name the extraction that reuse requires.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2d14023d701d7588","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan: 'Reuse a single documentation-gate definition shared with the full lane so ... cannot diverge'; AC 'The full Verify lane reuses the same documentation-gate definition'","norm_id":"ne6be35eda68b9850","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer, finding no shared definition to reuse, copy-pastes the doc-gate step list into a new docs-only job — reintroducing exactly the drift the plan says it prevents"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State that the changed-path classifier logic runs as trusted code from the default-branch workflow definition (not patchset-controlled), and that only the git changed-path LIST of the refspec is treated as untrusted data input.","cohort":["T5c"],"criteria":["T5c"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml lines 335-340: 'the vote decision must never run patchset-controlled code ... keeping the decision logic trusted also stops a change from voting itself Verified'","Plan: 'Keep ... all Gerrit security/trust boundaries unchanged' asserts the boundary is preserved but does not state WHERE the classifier runs relative to it","Reusable gate workflows 'inherit NO secrets' and check out the EXACT patchset — the classifier consuming that patchset's diff is the boundary-crossing input path"],"finding":"The plan adds a changed-path classifier whose output gates which security-relevant Verify checks run (feeding the Verified vote), but does not declare that the classifier logic itself must execute as TRUSTED code (from the default-branch workflow definition, not patchset-controlled input) — the same trust-placement the existing vote job enforces so a change cannot influence its own Verified vote.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb8b4e39d23703ce6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 'Add a deterministic changed-path classifier for the exact Gerrit patchset'; AC 'Verified voting remains fail-closed when the classifier or docs gate fails'","norm_id":"n096f81e8f1038e59","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A patch